{
  "_about": [
    "Hand-curated link between a spec's Parameters-table row and the place in a deployed run where the value actually used is recorded.",
    "This file is HUMAN/AGENT JUDGMENT, not a deterministic output. It was written on 2026-10-01 by reading the run scripts. Each entry says why the link is right.",
    "role: setting = a knob the executor chooses (null sizes, cell counts, thresholds); descriptor = a property of the source model or source data (e.g. layer numbers of an 18-layer model, anchor counts of the source paper) where a different value on MaxToki is expected and is NOT flagged; threshold = compare the numeric cut-off value itself; not_same_parameter = suppresses an automatic exact-name match that is a different setting.",
    "evidence: json = dotted key path suffix inside the run's output JSON (optionally limited by file_glob); script = a numeric constant name in the run's scripts (optionally limited by file_glob). Script values that are only defaults of environment variables are marked env_default by the checker; recorded JSON values take priority.",
    "spec_override: used only where the spec cell cannot be parsed but its meaning is plain; the raw text is kept in the output next to the override."
  ],
